  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Bridges: Prevent &amp; mitigate interreligious violence and promote peaceful co-existence in the Middle Belt of Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Intervening in the devastating violent inter-religious context of the Middle Belt region, CPI&#xbf;s proposal aims to prevent and mitigate inter-religious violence and promote peaceful co-existence among actors with different worldviews in Plateau, Nasarawa and Benue states by navigating the complex inter-ethnic/religious tensions. To this end, the proposed actions will focus on the urgent need to address the faith-based misconceptions by empowering gatekeepers, religious leaders, women and youth by providing a safe mediation space to conduct interfaith dialogue leading to the implementation of concrete joint actions, and by capacitating local faith-based CSOs and communities to promote peaceful interfaith relations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
